Upstream-Status: Pending
Exit: Drop alongside 0006 when fdsdk resolves the sandbox git-describe timeout at source.
Subject: python3-setuptools-scm: add VCS_VERSIONING_PRETEND_VERSION_FOR_SETUPTOOLS_SCM

Patch 0006 set SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION_FOR_SETUPTOOLS_SCM in the
element environment. Confirmed in the in-sandbox env dump (build log
"Build environment" section) that the var reaches the build. However,
build 9vclb still invoked git describe at build time, proving the var
was not consulted.

The reason: setuptools-scm's build backend has been migrating to
"vcs-versioning" (same repo, different package name, different env
namespace). When the backend used for THIS element is the
vcs-versioning variant, it reads VCS_VERSIONING_PRETEND_VERSION_FOR_X,
not SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION_FOR_X.

Add the VCS_VERSIONING_* equivalent alongside the existing var so the
override takes effect regardless of which backend path is used.
Version matches the element's ref (setuptools-scm-v10.3.4-0-gb27f...).

diff --git a/elements/components/python3-setuptools-scm.bst b/elements/components/python3-setuptools-scm.bst
--- a/elements/components/python3-setuptools-scm.bst
+++ b/elements/components/python3-setuptools-scm.bst
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@ variables:
 environment:
   # setuptools-scm#957 workaround: skip git-describe (times out in sandbox).
   SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION_FOR_SETUPTOOLS_SCM: "10.3.4"
+  VCS_VERSIONING_PRETEND_VERSION_FOR_SETUPTOOLS_SCM: "10.3.4"

 sources:
 - kind: git_repo
